    "content": "That's a great question about the referral process! Let me clarify how the system handles referrals based on the policy guidelines.\n\nAccording to the CRM policy, when a customer (in this case, your colleagues) asks to be recorded as a lead, you should call `create_person` with their name (and company if known). The policy states: \"Create the person first so you have their ID for later steps.\"\n\nSo the process would be:\n1. When your colleagues express interest through the referral opportunity, you would need to manually create a new lead record for each person using the `create_person` function\n2. The system doesn't automatically generate lead records - you need to create them manually\n3. Once you create the person record, you would then have their person ID to link them to the opportunity or create new opportunities as needed\n\nThis ensures that each referred person gets their own proper record in the system with their own relationship metrics (trust_level, commitment_level, lead_score, etc.) that can be tracked and managed individually.\n\nWould you like me to help you create a sample person record to demonstrate the process, or do you have any other questions about managing the referrals?",
